Ladybird maps valign on thead, tbody and tfoot to vertical-align now,
by parsing the attribute as a vertical-align value, as it already
did for tr, td and th. Blink does the same for all six elements in
HTMLTablePartElement::CollectStyleForPresentationAttribute(), and WebKit
in HTMLTablePartElement::collectPresentationalHintsForAttribute():
Both of them map the values top, middle, bottom and baseline to those
keywords, and take any other value as a vertical-align value. Gecko
parses valign with ParseTableVAlignValue() into one of those four
keywords only, in HTMLTableSectionElement::ParseAttribute(), and
maps it in nsGenericHTMLElement::MapTableVAlignAttributeInto(). So a
value such as sub or 10px applies in Ladybird, Chrome 158 and WebKit
26.5, and not in Firefox 151.
